# Line endings: LF in the repository and LF on checkout.
#
# Nothing in this tree wants CRLF. MSVC and PowerShell both read LF happily,
# while build_wsl.sh, scripts/*.sh and the PostToolUse hook are executed by WSL
# bash, which does not: a CRLF `set -euo pipefail` fails outright with
# "set: pipefail: invalid option name".
#
# Without this file git has no line-ending policy at all -- core.autocrlf is
# unset, so it stores whatever bytes it is handed. An editor that rewrote a
# source file with CRLF therefore turned a four-line edit into a whole-file
# diff, and 37 tracked files sat permanently "modified" for that reason alone.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary, never normalised. `text=auto` already detects these from their NUL
# bytes; naming them makes that independent of the heuristic.
*.bin    binary
*.qlbin  binary
*.glb    binary
*.gltf   binary
*.usdc   binary
*.usdz   binary
*.fbx    binary
*.exr    binary
*.png    binary
*.jpg    binary
*.jpeg   binary
*.qm     binary
